//! Loans, moves and regions in one typed body: borrow checking in the style of rustc's NLL.
//!
//! # When to use
//! Call [`check`] on a successfully typed, unselected body before it is published. A
//! [`Outcome.Conflict`] rejects the body with `LoanConflict` (`OWN0010`), `AccessDuringLoan`
//! (`OWN0011`), `ExpiredLifetime` (`OWN0019`), `UseAfterMove` (`OWN0001`), `OverlappingAssignment`
//! (`OWN0004`), `IncompatibleLoopHeader` (`OWN0005`), `ExtractionBoundary` (`OWN0002`),
//! `GuardConsumesPattern` (`OWN0008`) or `UnsatisfiedLifetimeBound` (`SEM0212`).
//! Every other body is proved: there is no partial verdict.
//!
//! # Details
//! The check numbers evaluation points in evaluation order and links them into a control-flow
//! graph. Every value has a type with region variables: each local, and each expression's result,
//! which lives from its evaluation to the node that consumes it. A value's variables are numbered
//! per distinct lifetime its type names (`Renumbering`). Lifetimes chosen outside the body (its own
//! and its enclosing declarations' lifetime parameters, `'static`, and the regions an anonymous
//! body's environment names) are universal; every other lifetime is the body's own.
//!
//! Wherever a value flows (a binding, an assignment, a call argument, a result, a return, a field
//! store, a capture) its type is related to the destination's structurally, by each position's
//! variance, adding outlives edges between variables (`relate`). A call instantiates the callee's
//! signature, which [`CallContract`] supplies, with fresh variables for the callee's own binders,
//! so the check never reads a callee body. A borrow creates a loan whose region is its reference's variable; a reborrow adds
//! that every reference it goes through outlives it.
//!
//! A region holds every point where a value whose type names it is live, plus what its outlives
//! edges add. A loan is in scope from its borrow while its region holds the point and its place is
//! not overwritten. Each access conflicts with the loans in scope it overlaps; the end of a local's
//! storage conflicts with every loan of it. A universal region that must outlive another universal
//! region needs a declared bound. Moves are checked on the same graph, independently of regions.
//!
//! An anonymous body does not own its by-reference captures: a loan of one reborrows through the
//! environment reference's region. A relation it needs between regions its creator chooses that its
//! premises do not prove is a requirement on its verdict (as rustc's closure region requirements);
//! the creator adds it between the regions the captured operands give them where it builds the
//! value, and reports what it breaks there.
//!
//! # Gotchas
//! Regions are location-insensitive (NLL): a holder keeps every loan stored in it alive while it
//! is live, even after the field holding it is overwritten. Location-sensitive regions are issue
//! #2022. Precision is per lifetime: two fields that share a lifetime parameter share its loans.

